ITEMS = ((('what is a sprain and how it happens', 'how do i treat a sprain', 'what is the first aid for a sprain', 'how to respond to a sprained ankle', 'what to do for a sprain at home', 'how do you handle a sprain', 'what helps a sprain for a sprain', 'how can i assist with a sprain', 'what is the best response to a sprain', 'how should i care for a sprain'), 'A sprain is an injury to a ligament, often from a twist. Rest the joint, support it with a bandage and use a cold pack wrapped in cloth to ease swelling. Ask a doctor or physiotherapist if pain or instability continues.'), (('what is a strain and how it happens', 'how do i treat a muscle strain', 'what is the first aid for a strain', 'how to respond to a strained muscle', 'what to do for a strain at home', 'how do you handle a strain', 'what helps a strain for a sprain', 'how can i assist with a strain', 'what is the best response to a strain', 'how should i care for a strain'), 'A strain is a stretched or torn muscle or tendon. Rest, gentle support and a wrapped cold pack can ease pain early on. Ask a doctor or physiotherapist if the area is very painful, weak or not improving.'), (('how do i know if it is a sprain or a fracture', 'can i tell a sprain from broken bone', 'what signs suggest a strain only', 'how to judge a twisted joint for a sprain', 'what if i cannot bear weight for a sprain', 'how to check for swelling and bruising for a sprain', 'what if the joint looks deformed for a sprain', 'when to get an x ray for a sprain', 'how to decide about medical help for a sprain', 'who can assess a joint injury for a sprain'), 'It can be hard to tell a sprain or strain from a fracture without an examination. If you cannot bear weight, the area is deformed or pain is severe, seek medical assessment. An x-ray may be needed.'), (('should i use ice on a sprain', 'how long to apply a cold pack to a strain', 'can i use heat for a sprain', 'what if the skin is numb for a sprain', 'should i wrap a cold pack for a sprain', 'how often can i cool an injured joint for a sprain', 'what helps swelling for a sprain', 'when to stop cooling for a sprain', 'what if cooling makes it worse for a sprain', 'who can advise on cold treatment for a sprain'), 'Use a cold pack wrapped in cloth for short periods to ease pain and swelling in a sprain or strain. Do not apply ice directly to the skin. Ask a pharmacist or doctor if the area becomes numb or pain increases.'), (('should i bandage a sprained ankle', 'how to support a strained muscle', 'what kind of bandage helps a sprain', 'how tight should a bandage be for a sprain', 'should i use a compression sleeve for a sprain', 'what if a bandage causes tingling for a sprain', 'how to check circulation after bandaging for a sprain', 'can i leave a sprain unsupported', 'how long to keep support on for a sprain', 'who can show me how to bandage for a sprain'), 'A supportive bandage can help a sprain or strain, but it should not be so tight that it causes tingling or cold fingers and toes. Ask a pharmacist or physiotherapist how to apply it, and get help if swelling increases.'), (('should i rest after a sprain', 'how soon can i walk on a strain', 'what if i need to keep moving for a sprain', 'should i elevate an injured limb for a sprain', 'how long to avoid sport for a sprain', 'what if the pain comes back for a sprain', 'how to return to activity safely for a sprain', 'what gentle movements are allowed for a sprain', 'when to ask about rehabilitation for a sprain', 'who can guide recovery for a sprain'), 'Rest the injured area at first and avoid activity that causes pain. Gentle movement can be introduced as it settles, guided by a physiotherapist. Ask a doctor if the joint feels unstable or pain returns.'), (('what can i take for sprain pain', 'should i use painkillers for a strain', 'can a pharmacist help with sprain pain', 'what if i am allergic to tablets for a sprain', 'should i use a pain relief gel for a sprain', 'what to avoid mixing for a sprain', 'how long to use pain relief for a sprain', 'what if pain is severe for a sprain', 'when to ask a doctor about medication for a sprain', 'who can advise on safe pain relief for a sprain'), 'Ask a pharmacist about suitable pain relief for a sprain or strain and follow the label. Do not use several products together without advice. Get medical help if pain is severe or the injury looks deformed.'), (('how do i treat a sprain in a child', 'can children get strains', 'what if a child limps after a twist for a sprain', "how to check a child's joint for a sprain", 'when to take a child to hospital for a sprain', 'how to comfort a child with a sprain', 'what if swelling spreads for a sprain', 'how long to rest a child for a sprain', "who can assess a child's injury for a sprain", 'what to tell the doctor for a sprain'), 'For a child with a sprain or strain, rest the area and use a wrapped cold pack. Seek medical assessment if they cannot bear weight, the joint looks odd or pain persists. Call emergency services for severe deformity.'), (('what if a sprain will not heal', 'how long does a strain take to settle', 'what if the joint keeps giving way for a sprain', 'should i see a physiotherapist for a sprain', 'what if swelling does not go down for a sprain', 'when to arrange an x ray for a sprain', 'what if pain moves elsewhere for a sprain', 'how to prevent another sprain', 'what exercises help for a sprain', 'who can review a slow recovery for a sprain'), 'Most sprains and strains improve with time and gradual movement, but persistent pain or instability needs assessment. A physiotherapist can advise on exercises. Ask a doctor if swelling continues or the joint feels unreliable.'), (('when should i call emergency services for a sprain', 'is a strain ever an emergency', 'what if a joint looks deformed with a strain', 'should i call for severe pain for a sprain', 'what if there is numbness for a sprain', 'how urgent is an injury with swelling for a sprain', 'what to report to the operator for a sprain', 'when to go to hospital for a sprain', 'how to keep the person still for a sprain', 'which paramedic takes over after a sprain'), 'Call emergency services for a deformed joint, severe pain, numbness or an injury with heavy bleeding. Tell the operator what happened and which joint is affected. Keep the person still until help arrives.'))
